[46.645379, "o", "PASSAGE_0000: WARNING: SIGNIFICANT DRUG INTERACTIONS WITH PAXLOVID - PAXLOVID includes ritonavir, a strong CYP3A i\r\nPASSAGE_0001: 1 INDICATIONS AND USAGE PAXLOVID is indicated for the treatment of mild-to-moderate coronavirus dise\r\nPASSAGE_0002: Limitations of Use PAXLOVID is not approved for use as pre-exposure or post-exposure prophylaxis for\r\nPASSAGE_0003: 2.1\tImportant Dosage and Administration Information PAXLOVID is nirmatrelvir tablets co-packaged wit\r\nPASSAGE_0004: 2.2\tRecommended Dosage The recommended dosage for PAXLOVID is 300 mg nirmatrelvir (two 150 mg tablet\r\nPASSAGE_0005: 2.3 Dosage in Patients with Renal Impairment Prescriptions should specify the numeric dose of each a\r\nPASSAGE_0006: Days of Treatment Dose and Dose Frequency PAXLOVID should be administered at approximately the same \r\nPASSAGE_0007: Days 1-5 150 mg nirmatrelvir (one 150 mg tablet) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) twice dai\r\nPASSAGE_0008: Day 1 300 mg nirmatrelvir (two 150 mg tablets) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) once\r\nPASSAGE_0009: Days 2-5 150 mg nirmatrelvir (one 150 mg tablet) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) once dail\r\nPASSAGE_0010: 2.4\tUse in Patients with Hepatic Impairment No dosage adjustment is needed in patients with mild (Ch\r\nPASSAGE_0011: 3 DOSAGE FORMS AND STRENGTHS PAXLOVID is nirmatrelvir tablets co-packaged with ritonavir tablets . -\r\nPASSAGE_0012: 4 CONTRAINDICATIONS PAXLOVID is contraindicated in patients with a history of clinically significant\r\nPASSAGE_0013: 5.1\tRisk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions Initiation of PAXLOVID, which contain\r\nPASSAGE_0014: 5.2\tHypersensitivity Reactions Anaphylaxis, serious skin reactions (including toxic epidermal necrol\r\nPASSAGE_0015: 5.3\tHepatotoxicity Hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice have occurred i\r\nPASSAGE_0016: 5.4\tRisk of HIV-1 Resistance Development Because nirmatrelvir is co-administered with ritonavir, the\r\nPASSAGE_0017: 6 ADVERSE REACTIONS The following clinically significant adverse reactions are described elsewhere i\r\nPASSAGE_0018: 6.1\tClinical Trials Experience Because clinical trials are conducted under widely varying conditions\r\nPASSAGE_0019: 7.1\tPotential for PAXLOVID to Affect Other Drugs PAXLOVID (nirmatrelvir co-packaged with ritonavir) \r\nPASSAGE_0020: 7.2\tPotential for Other Drugs to Affect PAXLOVID Nirmatrelvir and ritonavir are CYP3A substrates; th\r\nPASSAGE_0021: 7.3\tEstablished and Other Potentially Significant Drug Interactions Table 2 provides a listing of cl\r\nPASSAGE_0022: ↑ alfuzosin Co-administration contraindicated due to potential hypotension .\r\nPASSAGE_0023: ↑ tamsulosin Avoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID.\r\nPASSAGE_0024: ↑ ranolazine Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious and/or life-threatening \r\n[None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None]\r\n>>> "]
