[59.249777, "o", "PASSAGE_0000: 7.3\tEstablished and Other Potentially Significant Drug Interactions Table 2 provides a listing of clinically significant\r\nPASSAGE_0001: ↑ alfuzosin Co-administration contraindicated due to potential hypotension .\r\nPASSAGE_0002: ↑ tamsulosin Avoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID.\r\nPASSAGE_0003: ↑ ranolazine Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious and/or life-threatening reactions .\r\nPASSAGE_0004: ↑ antiarrhythmic Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for cardiac arrhythmias .\r\nPASSAGE_0005: ↑ antiarrhythmic Caution is warranted and therapeutic concentration monitoring is recommended for antiarrhythmics if ava\r\nPASSAGE_0006: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir Co-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resi\r\nPASSAGE_0007: Anticancer drugs abemaciclib, ceritinib,dasatinib, encorafenib,ibrutinib, ivosidenib, neratinib, nilotinib, venetoclax,v\r\nPASSAGE_0008: ↑ anticancer drugs Avoid co-administration of encorafenib or ivosidenib due to potential risk of serious adverse events \r\nPASSAGE_0009: ↑↓ warfarin Closely monitor international normalized ratio (INR) if co-administration with warfarin is necessary.\r\nPASSAGE_0010: ↑ rivaroxaban Increased bleeding risk with rivaroxaban. Avoid concomitant use. dabigatranSee Pharmacokinetics, Clinical \r\nPASSAGE_0011: ↑ dabigatran Increased bleeding risk with dabigatran. Depending on dabigatran indication and renal function, reduce dose\r\nPASSAGE_0012: ↑ apixaban Combined P-gp and strong CYP3A inhibitors increase blood levels of apixaban and increase the risk of bleeding\r\nPASSAGE_0013: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir Co-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resi\r\nPASSAGE_0014: ↑ anticonvulsant A dose decrease may be needed for clonazepam when co-administered with PAXLOVID and clinical monitoring\r\nPASSAGE_0015: ↓ bupropion and active metabolite hydroxy-bupropion Monitor for an adequate clinical response to bupropion.\r\nPASSAGE_0016: ↑ trazodone Adverse reactions of nausea, dizziness, hypotension, and syncope have been observed following co-administrat\r\nPASSAGE_0017: ↓ voriconazole Avoid concomitant use of voriconazole.\r\nPASSAGE_0018: ↑ ketoconazole↑ isavuconazonium sulfate↑ itraconazole Refer to ketoconazole, isavuconazonium sulfate, and itraconazole p\r\n"]
