[79.475228, "o", "1 Prescribing Information\r\n- 1 Medication Guide and Instructions for Use 1 Medication Guide and Instructions for Use\r\nStep 1: Remove the lopinavir and ritonavir oral solution bottle, bottle adapter, and oral syringe from the carton.\r\nStep 2: Open the bottle by pressing downward firmly on the child-resistant cap and twisting it in the direction of the arrow in the figure (counter-clockwise).\r\nDo not throw away the child-resistant cap.\r\nStep 3: Check the dose in milliliters (mL) as prescribed by your doctor. Find this number on the oral syringe.\r\nStep 5: Remove bottle cap and insert bottle adapter into bottle opening.\r\nInsert the oral syringe tip into the upright bottle through the opening of the bottle adapter until it is firmly in place.\r\nStep 6: With the oral syringe in place, turn the bottle upside down. Pull the plunger to withdraw the dose prescribed by your doctor (the amount of oral solution in Step 3).\r\nStep 9: Check that the correct dose was drawn up into the oral syringe.\r\nMeasure the dosage from the base of the plunger.\r\nIf the dose is not correct, insert the oral syringe tip firmly into the bottle adapter. Fully push in the plunger so that the oral solution flows back into the bottle.\r\nStep 10: Take the dose of lopinavir and ritonavir oral solution.\r\n- Swallow the lopinavir and ritonavir oral solution directly from the oral syringe.\r\nSwallow the lopinavir and ritonavir oral solution directly from the oral syringe.\r\n- Place the tip of the oral syringe in your mouth, point towards \r\n"]
