[149.990171, "o", "        \"answer\": \"Important warnings and precautions associated with Lopinavir-Ritonavir include: 1) Risk of serious and potentially fatal adverse reactions due to CYP3A-mediated drug interactions. 2) Toxicity in preterm neonates caused by ethanol and propylene glycol excipients in the oral solution, which has resulted in fatal cardiac toxicity, renal failure, and respiratory complications. 3) Pancreatitis (sometimes fatal), especially in patients with marked triglyceride elevations. 4) Hepatotoxicity, including transaminase elevations and hepatic dysfunction, particularly in patients with underlying chronic hepatitis B or C or cirrhosis. 5) QT interval prolongation"]
[150.078584, "i", " and torsade de pointes, necessitating avoidance in patients with congenital long QT syndrome or hypokalemia. 6) PR interval prolongation, which can lead to second or third-degree atrioventricular block, requiring caution in patients with structural heart disease or conduction system abnormalities.\",\n        \"citations\": [\n            {\n                \"set_id\": lop_rit_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0014\",\n                \"section\": \"5.1 Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Clinically significant adverse reactions, potentially leading to severe, life-threatening, or fatal events from greater exposures of concomitant medications.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": lop_rit_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0015\",\n                \"section\": \"5.2 Toxicity in Preterm Neonates\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Postmarketing life-threatening cases of cardiac toxicity (including complete AV block, bradycardia, and cardiomyopathy), lactic acidosis, acute renal failure, CNS depression and respiratory complications leading to death have been reported, predominantly in preterm neonates receiving lopinavir and ritonavir oral solution.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": lop_rit_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0016\",\n                \"section\": \"5.3 Pancreatitis\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Pancreatitis has been observed in patients receiving lopinavir and ritonavir therapy, including those who developed marked triglyceride elevations.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": lop_rit_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0017\",\n                \"section\": \"5.4 Hepatotoxicity\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"There have been postmarketing reports of hepatic dysfunction, including some fatalities. These have generally occurred in patients with advanced HIV-1 disease taking multiple concomitant medications in the setting of underlying chronic hepatitis or cirrhosis.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": lop_rit_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0018\",\n                \"section\": \"5.5 QT Interval Prolongation\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Postmarketing cases of QT interval prolongation and torsade de pointes have been reported although causality of lopinavir and ritonavir could not be established.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": lop_rit_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0019\",\n                \"section\": \"5.6 PR Interval Prolongation\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Lopinavir and ritonavir prolongs the PR interval in some patients. Cases of second or third degree atrioventricular block have been reported.\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"structured_fields\": {}\n    },\n    {\n        \"qid\": \"fbab4114f66e2dda\",\n        \"status\": \"ANSWERED\",\n        \"answer\": \"Important warnings and precautions associated with Paxlovid include: 1) Risk of serious, life-threatening, or fatal adverse reactions due to drug interactions with medications metabolized by CYP3A, or loss of therapeutic effect and viral resistance due to strong CYP3A inducers. 2) Hypersensitivity reactions, including anaphylaxis and serious skin reactions such as toxic epidermal necrolysis (TEN) and Stevens-Johnson syndrome (SJS), which require immediate discontinuation of the drug. 3) Hepatotoxicity, characterized by hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice, requiring caution in patients with pre-existing liver disease or enzyme abnormalities. 4) Risk of HIV-1 resistance development to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection, due to the co-administration of ritonavir.\",\n        \"citations\": [\n            {\n                \"set_id\": paxlovid_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0000\",\n                \"section\": \"WARNING: SIGNIFICANT DRUG INTERACTIONS WITH PAXLOVID\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"PAXLOVID includes ritonavir, a stro"]
[150.078613, "i", "ng CYP3A inhibitor, which may lead to greater exposure of certain concomitant medications, resulting in potentially severe, life-threatening, or fatal events\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": paxlovid_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0013\",\n                \"section\": \"5.1 Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Loss of therapeutic effect of PAXLOVID and possible development of viral resistance.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": paxlovid_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0014\",\n                \"section\": \"5.2 Hypersensitivity Reactions\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Anaphylaxis, serious skin reactions (including toxic epidermal necrolysis and Stevens-Johnson syndrome), and other hypersensitivity reactions have been reported with PAXLOVID .\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": paxlovid_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0015\",\n                \"section\": \"5.3 Hepatotoxicity\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice have occurred in patients receiving ritonavir.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": paxlovid_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0016\",\n                \"section\": \"5.4 Risk of HIV-1 Resistance Development\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Because nirmatrelvir is co-administered with ritonavir, there may be a risk of HIV-1 developing resistance to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection .\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"structured_fields\": {}\n    },\n    {\n        \"qid\": \"2d63e0a82215867f\",\n        \"status\": \"ANSWERED\",\n        \"answer\": \"The safety risks listed for Paxlovid include: 1) Serious, life-threatening, or fatal adverse reactions resulting from significant drug-drug interactions due to ritonavir, a strong CYP3A inhibitor, and potential loss of therapeutic efficacy or resistance due to CYP3A inducers. 2) Hypersensitivity reactions, including anaphylaxis and serious skin conditions such as Stevens-Johnson syndrome (SJS) and toxic epidermal necrolysis (TEN). 3) Hepatotoxicity, including clinical hepatitis, jaundice, and hepatic transaminase elevations, necessitating caution in patients with pre-existing liver disease or liver enzyme abnormalities. 4) Risk of HIV-1 developing resistance to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection, because nirmatrelvir is co-administered with ritonavir.\",\n        \"citations\": [\n            {\n                \"set_id\": paxlovid_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0000\",\n                \"section\": \"WARNING: SIGNIFICANT DRUG INTERACTIONS WITH PAXLOVID\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"PAXLOVID includes ritonavir, a strong CYP3A inhibitor, which may lead to greater exposure of certain concomitant medications, resulting in potentially severe, life-threatening, or fatal events\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": paxlovid_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0013\",\n                \"section\": \"5.1 Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Loss of therapeutic effect of PAXLOVID and possible development of viral resistance.\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": paxlovid_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0014\",\n                \"section\": \"5.2 Hypersensitivity Reactions\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Anaphylaxis, serious skin reactions (including toxic epidermal necrolysis and Stevens-Johnson syndrome), and other hypersensitivity reactions have been reported with PAXLOVID .\"\n            },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": paxlovid_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0015\",\n                \"section\": \"5.3 Hepatotoxicity\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, and jaundice have occurred in patients receiving ritonavir.\"\n      "]
[150.07865, "i", "      },\n            {\n                \"set_id\": paxlovid_set_id,\n                \"passage_id\": \"PASSAGE_0016\",\n                \"section\": \"5.4 Risk of HIV-1 Resistance Development\",\n                \"supporting_quote\": \"Because nirmatrelvir is co-administered with ritonavir, there may be a risk of HIV-1 developing resistance to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection .\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"structured_fields\": {}\n    }\n]\n\n# Validate supporting quotes\nprint(\"Validating quotes...\")\nfor ans in answers_data:\n    print(f\"Checking QID: {ans['qid']}\")\n    for cit in ans['citations']:\n        passage_text = get_passage(cit['set_id'], cit['passage_id'])\n        quote = cit['supporting_quote']\n        # Normalize whitespace for matching\n        norm_passage = \" \".join(passage_text.split())\n        norm_quote = \" \".join(quote.split())\n        if norm_quote not in norm_passage:\n            print(f\"ERROR: Quote not found in {cit['passage_id']}!\")\n            print(f\"Expected: {norm_quote}\")\n            print(f\"Passage: {norm_passage[:300]}...\")\n            exit(1)\n        else:\n            print(f\"  {cit['passage_id']} quote verified!\")\n\n# Save to /workspace/answers.json\nout = {\"answers\": answers_data}\nwith open('/workspace/answers.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\nprint(\"Answers written to /workspace/answers.json successfully!\")\nEOF\n"]
